From: EglantinePS5
Subject: up: EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET_PREPASS review fixes (T157): memory wait counted over the whole prepass, a fully known set skips the prepass, disk estimate counts the driver cache

Why (hostile review of 0770, 13 Nov 2026):
1. The prepass waited up to EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET_PREPASS_MEMORY_WAIT_S (300 s) under the memory floor
   per record: the wait started again from zero for every record, so memory that hovered at the
   floor could hold the boot for 300 s many times over. The wait is now counted over all records
   and passes of one prepass (ShaderSetPass::memory_waited); at 300 s in all the prepass ends and
   the game starts.
2. A start after a full pass read the whole set file again (one key-only read, about 6.5 s) and
   queued again every key whose build had thrown (a throw is not remembered as not keepable), at
   every start. The prepass now reads the "every record is known" marker first (the same test as
   PrepareShaderSet's) and ends at once when it holds.
3. The "Needs about N MB of disk" line counted the kept store only (21 KiB a key); it now adds
   about 7 KiB a key for the driver's own disk cache (estimate from 0484), which the disk floor
   only sees when it shares the file system.
Off: nothing changes (all three are inside the prepass, EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET_PREPASS=1).
Needs 0770 (and applies after 0771).
---
